Devices:
  * Implement several TTYs
  * Implement writing directly to serial console instead of VGA (like ttyS0)
  * [DONE] Implement block cache
  * Implement devfs (it seems not so difficult):
    - a separate virtual file system
    - define generic `dev_t` structure to contain necessary data about a device
    - maintain a list of registered devices
    - each device driver will register itself to the list of devices
    - implement file API (open, close, read, write)
    - implement directory API (readdir, open, lookup, etc.)
    - mount the filesystem in 'init' process code

